WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.729 --> 00:00:20.452
turned and saw Breckinridge shaking his fists at a little rat-faced man.

2
00:00:20.472 --> 00:00:23.014
"Those blasted geese!"

3
00:00:23.514 --> 00:00:24.375
the salesman shouted.

4
00:00:24.395 --> 00:00:28.378
"Don't bother me anymore, or I'll set my dog on you!

5
00:00:28.398 --> 00:00:30.359
I bought the geese from Mrs.

6
00:00:30.499 --> 00:00:31.680
Oakshott, not you."

7
00:00:32.924 --> 00:00:37.147
"No, but one was mine all the same," the little man whined.

8
00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.928
"Ask Mrs.

9
00:00:38.988 --> 00:00:39.708
Oakshott for it."

10
00:00:40.588 --> 00:00:41.809
"She said you had it."

11
00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:43.430
"Get out!"

12
00:00:44.311 --> 00:00:47.753
Breckinridge rushed toward him, but the little man ran away.

13
00:00:47.773 --> 00:00:52.775
"Ha! This may save us a trip," whispered Holmes.

14
00:00:53.776 --> 00:00:59.219
He raced through the crowd that had gathered, overtook the little man, and touched his shoulder.

15
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.201
Frightened, the rat-faced man turned around.

16
00:01:03.221 --> 00:01:04.422
"What do you want?"

17
00:01:04.822 --> 00:01:05.262
he croaked.

18
00:01:06.382 --> 00:01:10.664
"Excuse me," Holmes said, "but I overheard you at Breckinridge's.

19
00:01:11.485 --> 00:01:12.065
I can help."

20
00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:13.746
"Who are you?

21
00:01:14.526 --> 00:01:15.626
What could you know about it?"

22
00:01:16.927 --> 00:01:18.748
"My name is Sherlock Holmes.

23
00:01:19.368 --> 00:01:22.529
It is my business to know what other people don't know.

24
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.771
You're trying to trace some geese sold by Mrs.

25
00:01:26.871 --> 00:01:29.749
Oakshott to Breckinridge, which then went to Mr.

26
00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:31.190
Windigate at the Alpha.

27
00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.012
Windigate gave one to his club member Mr.

28
00:01:35.052 --> 00:01:35.772
Henry Baker."

29
00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:37.913
"You can help!"

30
00:01:38.594 --> 00:01:40.815
cried the little fellow, with quivering fingers.

31
00:01:42.176 --> 00:01:44.037
Sherlock Holmes hailed a passing cab.

32
00:01:44.057 --> 00:01:47.218
"We'd better talk somewhere quiet," he said.

33
00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:50.720
"But please, who are you?"

34
00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.242
The man hesitated for an instant.

35
00:01:54.282 --> 00:01:56.023
"My name is John Robinson."

36
00:01:57.104 --> 00:02:00.422
"No, your real name," Holmes said sweetly.

37
00:02:00.442 --> 00:02:03.743
"It's awkward doing business with an alias."

38
00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.565
The stranger's pale cheeks flushed.

39
00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:10.327
"Well my real name is James Ryder."

40
00:02:10.347 --> 00:02:14.169
"You are the hotel manager at the Cosmopolitan.

41
00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.150
Step in the cab please."

42
00:02:17.571 --> 00:02:22.874
The little man looked half frightened, half hopeful━not sure if he was on the verge of a windfall

43
00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:24.155
or a catastrophe.

44
00:02:25.255 --> 00:02:30.917
He entered the cab, and we rode in silence for thirty minutes until we were back at Baker

45
00:02:30.957 --> 00:02:32.638
Street and in the sitting room.

46
00:02:33.518 --> 00:02:34.098
"Here we are!"

47
00:02:34.758 --> 00:02:36.239
Holmes said cheerily as we entered.

48
00:02:36.259 --> 00:02:38.479
"A nice, warm fire.

49
00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.400
You look cold, Mr.

50
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.681
Ryder. Please take this chair.

51
00:02:43.661 --> 00:02:46.322
Now then, you want to know about those geese."

52
00:02:47.582 --> 00:02:49.002
"Yes, sir."

53
00:02:49.022 --> 00:02:50.743
"One particular goose actually.

54
00:02:51.423 --> 00:02:54.664
A white one with a black bar across the tail."

55
00:02:55.772 --> 00:02:57.153
Ryder quivered with emotion.

56
00:02:57.173 --> 00:03:00.596
"Oh," he cried, "where did it go?"

57
00:03:00.616 --> 00:03:02.277
"It came here.

58
00:03:02.998 --> 00:03:05.560
A most remarkable bird," said Holmes.

59
00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.282
"No wonder you're so interested.

60
00:03:08.883 --> 00:03:16.309
It laid an egg after it was dead━a very pretty and bright, little, blue egg."

61
00:03:17.189 --> 00:03:20.292
Our visitor staggered to his feet and clutched the mantelpiece.

62
00:03:21.513 --> 00:03:28.907
Holmes unlocked his safe and held up the Blue Carbuncle, shining like a star with a cold, brilliant,

63
00:03:29.307 --> 00:03:30.828
and many-pointed radiance.

64
00:03:32.109 --> 00:03:36.373
Ryder glared with a tense face, uncertain whether to claim or disown it.

65
00:03:36.393 --> 00:03:41.197
"The game is up, Ryder," Holmes said quietly.

66
00:03:42.057 --> 00:03:45.360
Ryder gasped and staggered like a zombie toward the stone.

67
00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:48.142
"Careful or you'll fall into the fire!

68
00:03:48.863 --> 00:03:50.404
Help him back to his chair, Watson.

69
00:03:51.485 --> 00:03:53.306
He doesn't have the nerve to be a thief.

70
00:03:54.187 --> 00:03:55.268
Give him a sip of brandy."

71
00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:00.883
Ryder sat back down with his brandy, but he stared ahead with frightened eyes.

72
00:04:00.903 --> 00:04:04.224
"Let's clear up some details, shall we?"

73
00:04:04.705 --> 00:04:05.165
Holmes said.

74
00:04:05.185 --> 00:04:10.328
"Mr. Ryder, how did you learn of the Countess of Morcar's blue stone?"

75
00:04:11.428 --> 00:04:12.509
Ryder's voice cracked.

76
00:04:12.529 --> 00:04:15.090
"Catherine Cusack told me about it."

77
00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:18.432
"I see━her ladyship's maid.

78
00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:24.735
You thought it would be so easy to give in to temptation and steal the gem, but you

79
00:04:24.795 --> 00:04:26.096
weren't very careful.

80
00:04:27.228 --> 00:04:32.890
You knew the plumber, Horner, had a criminal record and that suspicion would naturally fall on him.

81
00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:42.152
So you created some small job in the countess' room━you and your accomplice Cusack━and sent for Horner.

82
00:04:43.152 --> 00:04:49.554
After he left, you opened the jewel case, raised the alarm, and had that unfortunate man arrested.

83
00:04:50.394 --> 00:04:54.955
Then you━" Ryder threw himself down and clutched Holmes' knees.

84
00:04:55.716 --> 00:04:56.596
"Have mercy!"

85
00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:57.540
he shrieked.

86
00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.601
"Think of my family!

87
00:05:00.221 --> 00:05:01.262
It'll break their hearts.

88
00:05:02.262 --> 00:05:03.463
I never went wrong before!

89
00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.503
I never will again, I swear.

90
00:05:06.284 --> 00:05:07.124
Don't turn me in!

91
00:05:07.304 --> 00:05:08.245
Please, don't!"

92
00:05:08.265 --> 00:05:11.126
"Get back in your chair!"

93
00:05:11.706 --> 00:05:12.666
Holmes said sternly.

94
00:05:12.686 --> 00:05:18.409
"It's fine to beg now, but you didn't mind sending poor innocent Horner to prison."

95
00:05:18.429 --> 00:05:20.570
"I'll leave the country, Mr.

96
00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.271
Holmes! The charges against him will be thrown out."

97
00:05:23.291 --> 00:05:25.011
"We'll see.

98
00:05:26.572 --> 00:05:31.476
First how did the stone get into the goose, and how did the goose get sold?

99
00:05:32.037 --> 00:05:34.019
The truth is your only hope."

100
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.222
Ryder bit his parched lip.

101
00:05:37.242 --> 00:05:42.266
"I feared the police would search me and my room at the hotel, so I went to my

102
00:05:42.366 --> 00:05:45.469
sister's━Mrs. Oakshott of Brixton Road.

103
00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.531
She fattens geese.

104
00:05:48.492 --> 00:05:49.893
She said I seemed upset.

105
00:05:49.913 --> 00:05:52.496
‘Our hotel was robbed,' I told her.

106
00:05:53.476 --> 00:05:56.578
Then I went into her backyard and thought about what to do."

107
00:05:57.659 --> 00:05:59.240
He took a deep breath and continued.

108
00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:05.524
"An ex-convict friend of mine deals in stolen goods, and he said he could sell the gem for

109
00:06:05.584 --> 00:06:08.206
me. But how could I get it to him?

110
00:06:09.207 --> 00:06:12.389
I was worried I'd be searched and arrested with the stone in my pocket.

111
00:06:13.269 --> 00:06:19.414
Geese were waddling all around my feet, and suddenly I saw how I could fool the detectives."

112
00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:22.736
Ryder paused and shook his head.

113
00:06:23.748 --> 00:06:26.029
"My sister promised me a goose for Christmas.

114
00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:30.550
I'd take it now, I thought, and hide the stone inside it.

115
00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:36.452
I caught a fine, white goose with a bar on its tail, and I went behind the shed.

116
00:06:37.492 --> 00:06:43.033
I pried its bill open and thrust the stone down its throat as far as my finger could

117
00:06:43.113 --> 00:06:46.734
reach. The bird gulped, flapped, and struggled.

118
00:06:47.795 --> 00:06:51.896
When my sister came out, the bird broke loose and fluttered off among the others.

119
00:06:53.008 --> 00:06:53.808
"‘What are you doing?'

120
00:06:54.169 --> 00:06:54.669
she asked.

121
00:06:54.689 --> 00:06:57.250
"‘Finding the fattest,' I said.

122
00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.331
‘I'm picking out my Christmas gift.'

123
00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:02.532
"‘We put your bird aside already,' she said.

124
00:07:02.552 --> 00:07:06.994
"‘Thank you, Maggie,' I said, ‘but I prefer the one I just had.'

125
00:07:07.014 --> 00:07:09.415
"‘Yours is heavier,' she said.

126
00:07:09.435 --> 00:07:11.215
‘We fattened it just for you.'

127
00:07:11.235 --> 00:07:14.417
"‘No. I want the one I just had,' I said.

128
00:07:14.437 --> 00:07:16.958
"‘Fine,' she said, a little annoyed.

129
00:07:16.978 --> 00:07:17.938
‘Which one?'

130
00:07:17.958 --> 00:07:22.500
"‘That white one with the barred tail, right in the middle of the flock.'

131
00:07:23.436 --> 00:07:25.117
"‘Kill it and take it away,' she said.

132
00:07:25.137 --> 00:07:27.879
"I did and took it to my friend.

133
00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:32.521
We got a knife and opened the goose, but we couldn't find the stone.

134
00:07:33.562 --> 00:07:36.644
My heart turned to water at my terrible mistake.

135
00:07:37.664 --> 00:07:41.366
I rushed back to my sister's, but all the birds were gone.

136
00:07:42.407 --> 00:07:46.969
They had been taken to Breckinridge, so I asked my sister if there was another one with a

137
00:07:47.049 --> 00:07:47.910
bar on its tail.

138
00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.651
"‘Yes, there were two.

139
00:07:50.131 --> 00:07:51.292
I could never tell them apart.'

140
00:07:52.136 --> 00:07:55.779
"I pleaded with Breckinridge, but he wouldn't tell me where the geese went.

141
00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:57.981
My sister thinks I'm crazy.

142
00:07:59.202 --> 00:07:59.923
Perhaps I am.

143
00:08:00.523 --> 00:08:06.008
And now I'm branded a thief without ever touching the wealth I sold my character for!"

144
00:08:06.888 --> 00:08:11.012
He burst into convulsive sobbing and buried his face in his hands.

145
00:08:11.912 --> 00:08:18.738
We shared a long silence, broken only by Ryder's heavy breathing and the drumming of Sherlock Holmes' finger

146
00:08:18.878 --> 00:08:19.499
on the table.

147
00:08:20.439 --> 00:08:23.381
Then my friend rose and threw open the door.

148
00:08:23.401 --> 00:08:25.501
"Get out!"

149
00:08:26.101 --> 00:08:26.442
he said.

150
00:08:26.462 --> 00:08:28.822
"Oh! Heaven bless you!"

151
00:08:29.242 --> 00:08:29.822
cried Ryder.

152
00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.423
"No more words.

153
00:08:31.963 --> 00:08:32.503
Get out!"

154
00:08:33.624 --> 00:08:35.884
Ryder jumped up and clattered down the stairs.

155
00:08:36.944 --> 00:08:38.205
Holmes reached for his pipe.

156
00:08:38.225 --> 00:08:40.245
"We're not policemen after all.

157
00:08:41.206 --> 00:08:47.547
The countess will get her precious stone back, and Ryder won't testify, so Horner will soon go free.

158
00:08:48.468 --> 00:08:54.153
Look at it this way; I may be sidestepping the judge by not reporting this, but I'm also

159
00:08:54.253 --> 00:08:55.133
saving a soul.

160
00:08:56.114 --> 00:08:59.155
Send him to jail now, and he'll be a convict for life.

161
00:09:00.135 --> 00:09:02.976
Besides it's the season of forgiveness."

162
00:09:04.116 --> 00:09:05.276
"That's true," I said.

163
00:09:05.296 --> 00:09:13.178
"And now, my dear doctor," said Holmes, "let us tell the cook we are ready to enjoy a

164
00:09:13.298 --> 00:09:19.100
tastier investigation, in which a bird is also the chief feature."
